<title>USA: Nationwide Financial surges after IPO.</title>
<headline>Nationwide Financial surges after IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nationwide Financial, the life insurance business of Nationwide Insurance Enterprise, surged nearly 15 percent at its market debut after its $480 million initial public offering.</p>
<p>Shares rose 3-1/2 to 27. The IPO of 20.5 million shares priced above initial estimates, at $23.50 compared to an initial estimated pricing range of $21 to $23 a share. That range was raised to $23 to $24 a share by lead underwriter Credit Suisse First Boston.</p>
<p>The stock was the most actively traded issue on the New York Stock Exchange with nearly ten million shares traded in early afternoon.</p>
